### Store values and availability together (3/17)

**Severity:** `medium`

When a counter sample is missing, its previous value can look current. This member updates the data state with separate availability for dedicated and shared readings; apply all 17 suggestions together so each unavailable metric renders as `--`, not as measured zero.

```suggestion
        public bool DedicatedMemoryAvailable { get; private set; }

        public bool SharedMemoryAvailable { get; private set; }

        internal void UpdateMemorySample(AdapterMemorySample? sample)
        {
            var dedicated = sample?.Dedicated;
            var shared = sample?.Shared;
            DedicatedMemoryUsed = dedicated.GetValueOrDefault();
            SharedMemoryUsed = shared.GetValueOrDefault();
            DedicatedMemoryAvailable = dedicated.HasValue;
            SharedMemoryAvailable = shared.HasValue;
        }

        /// <summary>Gets or sets the utilization of each engine type the adapter has, in percent.</summary>
```

### Pass sample state to the template (11/17)

**Severity:** `medium`

When a counter sample is missing, its previous value can look current. This member provides independent sample flags for the template to hide only the unavailable counter bar; apply all 17 suggestions together so each unavailable metric renders as `--`, not as measured zero.

```suggestion
            ContentJson["hasSharedMemory"] = memory.SharedTotal > 0;
            ContentJson["hasDedicatedMemorySample"] = memory.DedicatedAvailable;
            ContentJson["hasSharedMemorySample"] = memory.SharedAvailable;
```

### Assert initial sample unavailability (16/17)

**Severity:** `medium`

When a counter sample is missing, its previous value can look current. This member asserts that an uninitialized memory sample is unavailable, preventing default zero values from looking like measured readings; apply all 17 suggestions together so each unavailable metric renders as `--`, not as measured zero.

```suggestion
        Assert.AreEqual(16UL, memory.SharedTotal);
        Assert.IsFalse(memory.DedicatedAvailable);
        Assert.IsFalse(memory.SharedAvailable);
```

### Cover valid, partial, and missing transitions (17/17)

**Severity:** `medium`

When a counter sample is missing, its previous value can look current. This member tests valid, partial, and absent samples and verifies that only the missing counter loses availability; apply all 17 suggestions together so each unavailable metric renders as `--`, not as measured zero.

```suggestion
    [TestMethod]
    public void UpdateMemorySample_ValidThenMissingAndPartialSamplesClearAvailability()
    {
        var data = new GPUStats.Data();

        data.UpdateMemorySample(new GPUStats.AdapterMemorySample(10, 20));

        Assert.IsTrue(data.DedicatedMemoryAvailable);
        Assert.IsTrue(data.SharedMemoryAvailable);
        Assert.AreEqual(10UL, data.DedicatedMemoryUsed);
        Assert.AreEqual(20UL, data.SharedMemoryUsed);

        data.UpdateMemorySample(new GPUStats.AdapterMemorySample(30, null));

        Assert.IsTrue(data.DedicatedMemoryAvailable);
        Assert.IsFalse(data.SharedMemoryAvailable);
        Assert.AreEqual(30UL, data.DedicatedMemoryUsed);
        Assert.AreEqual(0UL, data.SharedMemoryUsed);

        // A failed counter read returns no sample for this adapter.
        data.UpdateMemorySample(null);

        Assert.IsFalse(data.DedicatedMemoryAvailable);
        Assert.IsFalse(data.SharedMemoryAvailable);
        Assert.AreEqual(0UL, data.DedicatedMemoryUsed);
        Assert.AreEqual(0UL, data.SharedMemoryUsed);
    }

    [TestMethod]
```
